<title>UK: BT, Spain's Telefonica plan alliance - paper.</title>
<headline>BT, Spain's Telefonica plan alliance - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications Plc is planning a strategic alliance with Telefonica of Spain, the Financial Times said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The paper said BT was negotiating a stake in Telefonica Internacional (Tisa), Telefonica's international operation which has holdings in a few South American countries including Argentina, Chile and Peru.</p>
<p>A stake in Tisa would give BT and its American partner MCI a strong foothold in the South American market where neither is currently represented.</p>
<p>BT and MCI are in the course of a 12.5 billion pound ($19.9 billion) merger. Both of them are strong in Europe and North America.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717 ($ = 0.628 British Pounds)</p>
</text>
